messages:
olivia: FYI incoming from FinLedger — they want a BYOK setup that spans AWS KMS and Azure Key Vault. Primary asks: synchronized rotations, a single audit stream to their Splunk, and RBAC changes so their infra team can rewrap across accounts. Anyone done a cross-cloud rotation plan we can share?
jamal: short answer: we can support, but we don't have an automated cross-cloud rotation orchestration out of the box. rotation must be coordinated per cloud. key point: envelope encryption helps because we rotate the customer CMK/KeyVault key and only change the envelope key. but they asked for "synchronized" rotation — need to set expectations. :eyes:
serena: For onboarding checklist ask them for: key ARNs / key IDs, key policies (full JSON), allowed principals, service account emails, subscription/tenant IDs for Azure, and whether they want us to initiate rewrap or they'll call our API. Also request proof of log forwarding for audit (CloudTrail + Azure Activity Logs).
matt: tagging on docs gaps: our public BYOK guide doesn't have an example Key Vault access policy for a cross-tenant service principal. I'll open a docs task but for support here paste a minimal example they can use: 

```
// Azure Key Vault access policy snippet (example)
{
  "properties": {
    "accessPolicies": [
      {
        "tenantId": "<FINLEDGER_TENANT_ID>",
        "objectId": "<SERVICE_PRINCIPAL_OBJECT_ID>",
        "permissions": {
          "keys": ["wrapKey","unwrapKey","get"],
          "secrets": ["get"]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

jamal: For AWS KMS we need their key policy to include our cross-account kms:Encrypt/kms:Decrypt? Actually for rewrap we need kms:Encrypt and kms:ReEncrypt? The relevant actions are kms:Encrypt, kms:Decrypt, kms:ReEncrypt*, kms:GenerateDataKey. Recommend a key policy snippet with a dedicated role ARN we can assume.
serena: Also confirm rotation schedule: do they expect simultaneous rotation windows? If so, we should recommend a rolling plan: rotate Azure key first (short window), validate rewrap of envelopes, then rotate AWS key. Trying to do both at once increases chance of transient decryption failures.
olivia: They want zero-downtime and audit proof. Can we offer an automated fallback if rewrap fails on one side?
matt: We can implement a two-phase rollout in our onboarding runbook: 1) snapshot current envelope metadata, 2) perform test rewrap on a staging object, 3) run small production batch and verify decryption across services, 4) full rollout. We'll include automatic rollback markers if any rewrap returns non-200.
eng-ops-bot: Note created: SR-7643 onboarding ticket for FinLedger. Assigned: jamal, serena. Due: 2026-06-11. Actions: collect keys, policies, log sink details.
security-bot: Reminder: require audit retention >= 90 days for their compliance profile. Also enable immutable log export to customer Splunk bucket.
jamal: Action items for support message to customer: (1) Provide AWS key ARN, KMS key policy JSON, IAM role ARN for our service principal. (2) Provide Azure Key Vault name, tenant ID, service principal object ID + role assignment JSON. (3) Confirm audit log export destination (S3 or EventHub) and retention. (4) Confirm rotation cadence and maintenance windows.
serena: I'll draft the short checklist and a small runbook snippet we can paste in the ticket. I'll include the caveat: simultaneous cross-cloud rotation is not atomic; recommend staged rollout.
olivia: great — once Serena posts the checklist we'll PM FinLedger to collect items. Thanks all. :thumbsup:
